{"id": "10d60442-3448-4060-9550-14e21ec83913", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The opsai-bedrock-review skill explicitly excludes spend analysis, pointing instead to capacity-cost tooling, but that skill isn't available here. Still, figuring out which model is driving the Bedrock spend increase seems like a bounded cost-data question I can tackle via Cost Explorer through a sub-agent, rather than an open-ended root-cause investigation.

I'd call get_cost_and_usage grouped by usage type, filtered to Bedrock across the two months in question, noting that Bedrock third-party models like Claude show up under distinct service line items in Cost Explorer. I'll also need to check which accounts to include, possibly pulling associated accounts. I'll state my plan to the user first, then delegate this cost breakdown to a sub-agent with the use_aws tool preloaded, keeping it lightweight.

"}]}

{"id": "5a882c88-948a-48da-bd5d-a0cbd07dbf3e", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll break down last month's Bedrock cost by model and usage type and compare it with the month before. Then I'll look at what that points to for cutting spend.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_HTbdCfsGIK6wu2dfOkIEIp", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-cost-breakdown", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["verifying-with-docs", "searching-logs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Identify which Amazon Bedrock model(s) and usage types drove a roughly 2x increase in Bedrock spend last month (October 2026) versus the prior month (September 2026), and propose concrete cost-reduction options.",
  "context": "User says their Amazon Bedrock bill doubled last month and wants to know which model is driving spend and how to cut it. Current date is 2026-11-25. This is a read-only cost analysis. Use AWS Cost Explorer (ce get_cost_and_usage, region us-east-1) in the agent space account 012345678901_1 and any other associated AWS accounts (use list_associations to find them; check whether the account is a payer/linked account). Note that third-party models on Bedrock (e.g. Anthropic Claude) often bill under separate SERVICE names such as 'Claude (Amazon Bedrock Edition)', 'Amazon Bedrock', etc., so include all services with 'Bedrock' in the name, not just 'Amazon Bedrock'. Model, region and input/output token breakdowns are usually visible in USAGE_TYPE (e.g. 'USE1-<Model>-input-tokens', 'output-tokens', provisioned throughput, batch, cache, custom model storage/training, guardrails, knowledge base).",
  "resources": ["Cost Explorer", "Amazon Bedrock", "CloudWatch namespace AWS/Bedrock", "Bedrock model invocation logging if enabled"],
  "timeframe": "Compare 2026-09-01/2026-10-01 vs 2026-10-01/2026-11-01 (monthly), plus daily granularity for October-November 2026 to find when the increase started and whether it is ongoing.",
  "criteria": "1) Total Bedrock cost per month and % change. 2) Top cost contributors by SERVICE and USAGE_TYPE (model, input vs output tokens, provisioned throughput, etc.), with the delta vs prior month; name the model(s) responsible for most of the increase. 3) Daily trend: step change vs gradual growth, and the date it began. 4) If feasible, attribute spend to callers/applications (CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock InvocationCount/InputTokenCount/OutputTokenCount by ModelId, cost allocation tags, or invocation logs by IAM identity) but do not go deep. 5) Cost-reduction recommendations tied to the actual findings (e.g. cheaper model tier, prompt caching, batch inference, provisioned throughput right-sizing or idle provisioned throughput, shorter outputs/max_tokens, cross-region inference profiles, retry loops). Keep it shallow: give figures and suggest deeper areas rather than exhaustively investigating. Report concrete numbers. Do not write the raw 12-digit account ID in your report; refer to accounts by alias or last 4 digits."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Analyze Bedrock cost by model with Cost Explorer"}], "created_at": null}

